@baseUrl = http://localhost:5229
# For deployed Render URL, replace @baseUrl with your render URL, e.g.:
# @baseUrl = https://dailypractice-aspdotnet-api.onrender.com

### ==============================================================================
### 1. CENTRALIZED REUSABLE PAGINATION API (GET & POST)
### ==============================================================================

### 1a. Default Pagination (Page 1, PageSize 10)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/paginated
Accept: application/json

### 1b. Page 2 with PageSize 5
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/paginated?pageNumber=2&pageSize=5
Accept: application/json

### 1c. Missing PageNumber and PageSize (Automatically defaults to Page 1, PageSize 10)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/paginated?searchTerm=
Accept: application/json

### 1d. Invalid / Negative PageNumber & PageSize (Automatically normalized: PageNumber=1, PageSize=10)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/paginated?pageNumber=-5&pageSize=-20
Accept: application/json

### 1e. PageSize Greater than 100 (Clamped to Max allowed 100)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/paginated?pageNumber=1&pageSize=500
Accept: application/json

### 1f. Search across multiple fields (e.g. name, email, address, role)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/paginated?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10&searchTerm=john
Accept: application/json

### 1g. Filter by Role ID (e.g. role_id = 2 for Users) + Sort Ascending by FirstName
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/paginated?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10&role_id=2&sortBy=firstName&sortDirection=asc
Accept: application/json

### 1h. Empty Results (SearchTerm with zero matches returns TotalRecords=0 and TotalPages=0)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/paginated?searchTerm=NonExistentUserXYZ99999
Accept: application/json

### 1i. POST Paginated Endpoint with JSON Payload
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/paginated
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pageNumber": 1,
  "pageSize": 10,
  "searchTerm": "",
  "sortBy": "createdDate",
  "sortDirection": "desc"
}

### ==============================================================================
### 1j. FETCH ALL USERS API (Unpaginated - Backwards Compatible)
### ==============================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/fetch_users
Accept: application/json

### Or using RESTful convention:
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users
Accept: application/json

### ==============================================================================
### 2. ADD USER API (Binary Photo Upload via multipart/form-data)
### Returns user with numeric digit ID (1, 2, 3...)
### ==============================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/add_user
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="first_name"

John
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="middle_name"

Robert
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="last_name"

Doe
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="role_id"

2
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="password"

Password123!
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="address"

123 Main Street, Suite 400, New York
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="mobile_no"

+1-555-0199
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="email_id"

john.doe@example.com
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photo"; filename="profile.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./profile.jpg
--WebAppBoundary--

### ==============================================================================
### 2b. ADD USER API (Option B: JSON with optional Base64 binary photo)
### ==============================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/add_user
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "first_name": "Jane",
  "middle_name": "Marie",
  "last_name": "Smith",
  "role_id": 2,
  "password": "Password123!",
  "address": "456 Broadway, New York",
  "mobile_no": "+1-555-0188",
  "email_id": "jane.smith@example.com"
}

### ==============================================================================
### 3. GET SINGLE USER BY DIGIT ID API
### ==============================================================================
@userId = 1

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/{{userId}}
Accept: application/json

### ==============================================================================
### 4. GET USER PHOTO (Raw Binary Image Stream)
### Returns binary image data (Content-Type: image/jpeg, image/png)
### Directly viewable in browser or inside <img src="/api/Users/1/photo" />
### ==============================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/{{userId}}/photo

### ==============================================================================
### 5. DEDICATED BINARY PHOTO UPLOAD / UPDATE API
### Uploads or replaces raw binary photo for an existing user by digit ID
### ==============================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/{{userId}}/upload_photo
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photo"; filename="avatar.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./avatar.png
--WebAppBoundary--

### ==============================================================================
### 6. DELETE USER PHOTO API
### Removes binary photo data from database and deletes disk cache
### ==============================================================================
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/{{userId}}/photo
Accept: application/json

### ==============================================================================
### 7. EDIT / UPDATE USER API (JSON)
### ==============================================================================
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/edit_user/{{userId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "first_name": "John",
  "middle_name": "Robert",
  "last_name": "Smith",
  "role_id": 2,
  "password": "NewSecurePassword456!",
  "address": "789 Park Avenue, Floor 10, New York",
  "mobile_no": "+1-555-0200",
  "email_id": "john.smith@example.com"
}

### ==============================================================================
### 8. DELETE USER API (POST method with user_id in payload)
### ==============================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/delete_user
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": 1
}

### Or using DELETE HTTP verb:
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/delete_user/{{userId}}
Accept: application/json

### ==============================================================================
### 9. GET ALL ROLES API
### ==============================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/roles
Accept: application/json

### ==============================================================================
### 10. LOGIN API (Authenticate & obtain JWT Bearer token + user profile with digit ID)
### ==============================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### ==============================================================================
### 11. REQUEST LOGIN OTP (via ZeptoMail)
### ==============================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/send-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com"
}

### ==============================================================================
### 12. VERIFY OTP & LOGIN (Get JWT Bearer Token)
### ==============================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/login-with-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "otp": "123456"
}
